# With an `or`, the `and` fix would regroup the conditions: not machine-applicable (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
from T | where a or b, c
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..25
  PIPELINE@0..24
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "T"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..24
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..21
        NAME_REF@15..16
          IDENT@15..16 "a"
        WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
        OR_KW@17..19 "or"
        WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
        NAME_REF@20..21
          IDENT@20..21 "b"
      COMMA@21..22 ","
      WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
      NAME_REF@23..24
        IDENT@23..24 "c"
  WHITESPACE@24..25 "\n"

error[DS0115]: `where` takes one condition
  --> query:1:22
  |
1 | from T | where a or b, c
  |                      ^ a comma does not join conditions
  |
  = help: combine the conditions with `and`: `a or b and c`
